{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Visits Vanessa at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Grabbing Dinner "}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking about Wishes and Imaginary Situations  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class =\"italic\">\u201cI wish ... \u201d</span> to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The verb <span class =\"italic\">wish</span> introduces an idea. It is something that is not true, but you could like to be true."}, {"type": "text", "content": "After <span class =\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"italic\">I wish I knew ... <br/>I wish I had ... <br/>I wish you were ... </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br/> Wish + past tense"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish it was a weekday.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I want it to be a weekday, but it is a weekend.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish I knew more about design. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I want to know about design, but I don't.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish we were going to Ned's.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I want to go to Ned's, but I'm not going there.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish we served lobster!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would like us to serve lobster, but we don't.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs with \u201cGo\u201d  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A phrasal verb is a phrase formed with a verb + preposition.  <br/><br/>The combination of the verb and preposition changes the meaning of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Many phrasal verbs start with the verb <span class =\"italic\">\u201cgo\u201d</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "to go out -- to leave the house<br/>to go by -- to pass an amount of time<br/>to go with -- to match, to be well suited<br/>to go over -- to study, to read carefully<br/>to go along -- to accept, agree<br/>to go off -- to ring or sound out, like a bell or whistle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You conjugate phrasal verbs in the same way you conjugate other verbs."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Question Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I go out on Saturdays.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you go out on Saturdays?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am going out this evening.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Are you going out this evening?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Continuous tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I went out last Saturday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Did you go out last Saturday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I have gone out every Saturday this month.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have you gone out every Saturday this month?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect tense\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I can't believe six months have gone by!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The designer went over her plans."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The mural on the wall goes with the design."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "design"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way an object or environment appears, after careful thought and planning"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I wish I knew more about design. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about social activities."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to grab dinner"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have an informal dinner with someone, usually a friend "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm glad we decided to grab dinner at your restaurant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mural"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very large image (painting, photograph, etc.), usually painted on a wall or in a public space"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The mural on the wall goes well with the design."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lighting"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way lights (lamps, etc.) look, where they are placed and how much light they give in an area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I love the design. The lighting is perfect."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "live music"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "people playing musical instruments and singing before an audience"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  We're going to listen to some live music. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "band"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of musicians playing together, usually including people playing instruments or singing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We're going to listen to some live music. A new band is playing.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le07ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prepare 10 small cards with true and imaginary statements about your life. Use the Present tense. For example, you can write:  <span class=\"italic\">I speak English. I go to Florida every year. I live in New York.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your partner to prepare 10 more cards."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Mix up the 20 cards and place them face down."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Pick one of the cards. Make a sentence with the information on the card. Start with: <span class=\"italic\">It's true that...</span> if it is true or <span class=\"italic\">I wish...</span> if it is not true.  Explain why you made that sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your partner picks a card and does the same thing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Continue the game until there 